# GitHub's language bar weighs bytes of committed files, and this repository
# commits its own outputs: a self-contained HTML research report with charts and
# data embedded in it. Left unmarked, that one file makes the project look like
# 89% HTML when the work is Python, SQL and MATLAB.
#
# Marking them keeps the artifacts in the repository — the case study links the
# report — while excluding them from the language statistics and collapsing them
# in diffs, which is also what you want when reviewing a change.

outputs/**              linguist-generated=true
docs/**                 linguist-documentation=true
data/*.csv              linguist-generated=true

# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout does not rewrite every file.
* text=auto eol=lf
